I use AI tools every day. At some point, that stopped being enough.

I needed to know how a machine generates coherent responses to anything, instantly.

So I went back to the beginning. Not by reading — by building.

Every concept behind modern LLMs. From scratch. One at a time.

Perceptron → MLP → Backpropagation → CNN → ResNets → RNN → Attention → Transformer

Each step answered what the last one couldn't.

I didn't follow a course. I built what I needed to understand, watched it break, and figured out why it works.

By the end, I could trace every component in a Transformer — because I'd built it myself.

